 ## Overview
-Marching Cubes with Topological Correction (Case 6c) is a variant of the Marching Cubes algorithm that resolves topological inconsistencies (holes) in the extracted isosurface by applying an alternate facetization for specific cube configurations. It specifically addresses the topological error that occurs when a Case 3 cube is adjacent to a Case 6 cube, ensuring the resulting surface is manifold and continuous. It differs from standard Marching Cubes by detecting this specific adjacency and swapping the triangle connectivity for the Case 6 cube, and differs from [Marching Cubes 2](1393-marching-cubes-2.md) by focusing on this specific topological correction rather than a general lookup table reimplementation.
+Marching Cubes with Topological Correction (Case 6c) is a variant of the Marching Cubes algorithm that resolves topological inconsistencies (holes) in the extracted isosurface by applying an alternate facetization for specific cube configurations [S1, unofficial]. It specifically addresses the topological error that occurs when a Case 3 cube is adjacent to a Case 6 cube [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard Marching Cubes by detecting this specific adjacency and swapping the triangle connectivity for the Case 6 cube, and differs from [Marching Cubes 2](1393-marching-cubes-2.md) by focusing on this specific topological correction rather than a general lookup table reimplementation [S1, unofficial].
 
